<title>USA: Doubletree files for $230 mln share offer.</title>
<headline>Doubletree files for $230 mln share offer.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Doubletree Corp, in a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, said on Tuesday it intended to make an offering of common stock to raise up to $230 million.</p>
<p>The hotel operator, based in Phoenix, will use net proceeds from the offering to help finance the acquisition of Red Lion Hotels Inc, Doubletree said.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through an underwriting group led by Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc, Doubletree said.</p>
